      "content": "Libertarians ground their opposition to progressive taxation in the natural rights theory of John Locke, arguing that the state has no moral authority to seize private property for redistribution without explicit, consensual consent from every individual. In contrast, social democrats rely heavily on the utilitarian and \"active citizenship\" frameworks, positing that a full guarantee of civil liberties and social stability achieved through redistribution outweighs the strictures of absolute property ownership. To maintain balance in your paper, consider highlighting how libertarians view modern tax policy as a systemic violation of individual autonomy, while social democrats argue it is an essential mechanism for mitigating societal inequities and fostering genuine freedom for all citizens.",
